it has been a very eventful few weeks  for division fans with the three stages  of pts wrapping up the sudden  announcement of title update 15 being  released on the 12th of may and a state  of the game stream led by creative  director yannick and community developer  daria  in this video i'm going to cover what  was discussed on stream and what we have  to expect in this new update including  the new story direction  [Music]  [Music]  they were quick to reaffirm would have  been stated quite a while ago where  title update 12 was initially meant to  be the last update to the game but due  to good interaction it was decided that  more content was to be added however  this didn't mean that they could just  jump back in as normal the vast majority  of the original team had been moved on  to new projects so a lot of time was  placed on reassembling a team and  setting up a new development process  title update 15 isn't necessarily the  outcome of the last 12 months worth of  work but rather a small piece of the  long-term support with more seasons and  content to come  the pts was just one of the many ways of  which they have started to reinstate  their communication with the community  it was a good way to get the  conversation going and get an  understanding of the hopes and dreams  the community had in mind  overall the pts has been considered a  success with around 19 000 players  participating  there has been a lot of feedback  including the countdown mode and the  expertise system  as a quick recap countdown is the new  game mode where eight division agents  work together to restore stability to a  power plant that is infested with  enemies and other hazards you have just  15 minutes to prevent a lockdown  deployed in teams of four at different  locations you will need to complete a  series of objectives and then extract  before the time runs out  although it is intended for eight  players it can be completed with less  and there is matchmaking  running through the feedback received a  number of the changes had already been  made by the end of the pts but they are  still looking into the difficulty  options and how this could be scaled for  more experienced teams  for now they are happy with how it is  but will continue to take feedback once  it launches to the rest of the player  base  also discussed with the expertise system  this is a new way to upgrade items  players can build their expertise by  using any item in the game as they use  items they'll become more proficient  with them  once they've maxed out their proficiency  rank with any item type they'll be able  to upgrade its base stats  basically it's a new way for players to  increase their power  the majority of the feedback from the  pts was that it takes too long or costs  too many materials to upgrade items  while the costs have been significantly  reduced the expertise system wasn't  intended to be another activity that  players can power level through as they  stated on the stream this is to be more  of a passive activity much like the  watch  it's more of a slow burn in the  background while working on other things  those in the community screaming out  that it's too slow seem to have missed  the point however the question around  why we need to increase our power level  when the current difficulty is staying  as is is something that still hasn't  been answered  in the stream they also told us of  upcoming season hidden alliance this  will feature a new main target captain  lewis as well as two new apparel events  new reward track and an addition to the  story  following the death of antoine ridgeway  a new leader has risen to take control  they've also set larger goals of moving  their operation nationwide  one leader known as captain lewis has  descended upon washington dc with a  mission of his own  accompanying lewis will be a number of  lieutenants  castillo a civilian turned true son he  has a background in engineering and is  taking over radio frequencies where he  sends out his rants that are being used  as a recruiting tool  daniels this woman is on a rampage and  is assassinating civilians in the  streets  chang a logistical nightmare that has  been so effective in rebuilding supply  chains for the true sons that has become  a major problem  and xander who has been randomly  torturing and interrogating civilians it  is not known what she is actually  looking to find but she has to be  stopped  in their words the new lieutenants and  prime target himself range from  monstrous to sympathetic the ideology  and tactics of the true sons have  changed which in turn starts to alienate  some of their most zealous members while  attracting a new wave of cruel  opportunists with an eye to join an  oppressive army of the powerful  the internal struggles of this new  generation of true sons will shine a  light on the complexities of the world  in turmoil and will provide the first  glance at a new threat rising to  prominence  i'm liking the sounds of this it's like  we'll be seeing a more gritty story  behind the true suns and the state of  the world around them rather than the  straight good versus evil storyline  we've had with a few of the targets up  until now  it looks like we'll be getting a bit of  depth on the inner workings and  complications with the characters and  the true suns organization as well as  what's happening around them  could almost say it feels similar to  some of the stories we were getting in  the original game  although season 9 will be a direct  continuation of where we left off they  use the opportunity to clarify one thing  that feylau is indeed dead  however the consequences of what faye  did will be cleared up  questions like why did she go rogue why  did she kill the president and then  blame the division these will be  answered  they've also stated that the way the  story will be told will be taking a  change in direction  the core message and plot of the  division will no longer be locked behind  a number of collectibles that need to be  pieced together in order to understand  what is going on  hidden alliance will open with a  cinematic showing the outcome following  the confrontation with fey lau at camp  white oak  the story then shifts over kalso benitez  and rhodes who are all coping with what  has happened in their own ways  the addition of cinematic language will  make the stakes in motivation crystal  clear and moved out of the darkness  this new approach has been taken to show  the changing motivation and feelings of  core characters  collectibles will still be available but  these will be easier to obtain by  meeting with kelso at the base of  operations after each manhunt target has  been eliminated  the idea is that this more focused  delivery will help players avoid missing  critical story details  while i find this interesting i just  hope we don't lose everything that the  collectibles gave  i completely agree the majority of  players would like a clear and upfront  story most of these don't want every  detail just the basics the reason for  the collectibles in a lot of games  destiny 2 for example is to provide the  extra detail behind the story and  building of the world without annoying  the players who don't care for it  i'll admit i'm skeptical of this change  but i'm happy for them to be trying  something new as long as we don't lose  any detail  the manhunt structure has also been  tweaked to provide a stronger narrative  rather than exploring every district of  washington the focus will be placed on a  much smaller area giving the opportunity  to provide more contained concentrated  stories and to avoid repetition from  season to season  there has been more flexibility and  variety added to the manhunts too  manhunt lieutenants will each take over  a main mission from the dc campaign  these mission takeovers will become more  common in future seasons as they expand  the capabilities of the system  for now cedar's mission is being  repopulated with true sons who have  taken control for their own purposes  and it goes without saying that we'll be  seeing new weapons and gear including a  heartbreaker gear set new exotic and  named weapons and more  a while ago we were introduced to an  intelligence annex that discussed major  changes to the specialization system  they understand that these aren't really  working as well as they could be most  people just picked the specialization  based on the buffs they were after and  then forget about them  they've been working on a revamp that  would have more meaningful choices to be  made to have a larger impact on your  playstyle to have you make choices that  force you to gain in something but miss  out on another  so this revamp had always been planned  for release with the title 15 update but  they have decided to push it back into a  later update they aren't quite ready  at the end of the stream they took  questions from the community now there  are a whole bunch of them so i've only  summarized the ones that i've also  received a number of questions about  over the last 12 months  when will we have crossplay this is not  something they are looking into at the  moment essentially the way each system  has been set up with separate databases  per platform there is no simple way for  them to flip a switch and have them all  communicate with each other in order for  them to get cross-play working they  would need to dedicate a large team to  have this work within any reasonable  time and currently the team is working  on new content  game crashes in the game the pts crashes  have been fixed and addressed as for the  live crashes they plan on addressing  these in the next update  will there be another dlc there are no  plans to add paid dlcs they plan to  continue with the season and season pass  model as they have been since warlords  of new york  will there be focus on pvp they  understand there is a passionate pvp  community out there but the current team  they have is specialized in pve content  they don't want to give up on pvp since  it's a big part of the game but at the  moment there is no pvp 2.0 patch planned  but they will be keeping an eye on the  big issues and try to address them one  step at a time  will you add more map locations  countdown is essentially a new map  location  map expansions like warlords of new york  are not in the plan at the moment but  there are new maps and new spaces that  you can discover through different types  of content that will be coming out  will there be more legendary missions  the expertise in specialization revamp  will make players more powerful raids  and legendary missions are currently the  most difficult content  adding more legendary missions could be  an option but adding legendary  difficulty to new content is not like  flipping a switch it is handcrafted and  balanced by the developers  the real question is how do you make the  game challenging and interesting for the  players and that needs to be answered  smartly  will you consolidate the dark zones  there are no plans to merge the dark  zones but they are looking into general  topics on how to improve the dark zone  summing up on the 12th of may we'll be  receiving the following a new game mode  called countdown a new leveling system  called expertise manhunt hidden alliance  featuring an alternative way of telling  the story and running through the  targets a new season reward track new  items including weapons gear exotics  named items and gear set  but like i've said before the one piece  i'd like everyone to take away from this  probably the most important piece is  that this is just one of many updates  that we'll be receiving through 2022  there is more to come  beyond that who knows as yannick said  himself during the stream it all depends  on what sort of engagement the game gets  over the next year that will determine  what sort of support will be thrown  their way in the future  anyway thank you very much for watching  not long until the update releases now  so see you in dc  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  cheers okay

